@@ -1012,8 +1012,14 @@ public static String getShortCanonicalName(final String canonicalName) {
      * Gets the class name minus the package name from a {@link Class}.
      *
      * <p>
-     * This method simply gets the name using {@code Class.getName()} and then calls {@link #getShortClassName(String)}. See
-     * relevant notes there.
+     * This method uses {@link Class} metadata to correctly handle {@code $} characters in valid class identifiers,
+     * which may appear in top-level classes (e.g., {@code $trange}), member classes (e.g., {@code Outer.$Inner}),
+     * or nested identifiers (e.g., {@code Outer.Inner.Ne$ted}).
+     * </p>
+     *
+     * <p>
+     * For local and anonymous classes, this method falls back to string-based parsing to preserve compiler-generated
+     * ordinal naming expected by existing tests.
